  "text": "⚟\nTo simplify the expression \\(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + \\sqrt[3]{8}}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}}\\), we start by recognizing that \\(\\sqrt[3]{8} = 2\\). This allows us to rewrite the expression as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}}\n\\]\n\nWe need to rationalize the denominator. To do this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, \\(\\sqrt[3]{9^2} + \\sqrt[3]{9} \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{6^2}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2}{\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{9^2} + \\sqrt[3]{9} \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{6^2}}{\\sqrt[3]{9^2} + \\sqrt[3]{9} \\sqrt[3]{6} + \\sqrt[3]{6^2}}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{(\\sqrt[3]{4} + 2)(\\sqrt[3]{81} + \\sqrt[3]{54} + \\sqrt[3]{36})}{(\\sqrt[3]{9} - \\sqrt[3]{6})(\\sqrt[3]{81} + \\sqrt[3]{54} + \\sqrt[3]{36})}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\sqrt[3]{9^2} = \\sqrt[3]{81}\\), \\(\\sqrt[3]{9 \\cdot 6} = \\sqrt[3]{54}\\), and \\(\\sqrt[3]{6^2} = \\sqrt[3]{36}\\), we want to see that these terms are zeros in the denominator when expanded, thus giving us a simpler solution:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{4896} - \\sqrt[3]{162} + \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{166384}, -2 + \\frac{\\sqrt{2} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\sqrt[t]{2}} - \\frac{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}}}{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{4}}} - \\frac{-\\sqrt[3]{8}}{\\sqrt[3]{9}}}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified answer is \\(\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4896} + \\sqrt[3]{162}}{\\sqrt[3]{86286}}\\), and therefore \\(\\boxed{4494}\\).",
